{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he moved on.</b> From the heavy [intensive] conjugation, the augmented form, and it is a transitive verb: for 'and a rock moves from its place' (Job 18:4) stands [intransitively], while 'Oholah' and also 'Ohaliv' — the meaning of ויעתק is 'and he journeyed.' The nun is absent after the yod, and a tav stands in place of the nun, for it is [of] the form פָּעַל, and likewise וַיֵּז נִצְחָם (Isaiah 63:3). And both are transitive verbs." "And the meaning of 'Ai' is to the west, for to the west of the Land of Israel is the Great Sea, the Spanish [Sea], and it is not the Ocean, for the aforementioned land is far from it. And he traveled from east of Bet El westward until Ai was east of his camp." "And the meaning of 'and he called in the name of YHWH' is prayer, or calling people to worship HaShem."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:36.170534009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}